          %title Gauge symmetries
          %h2#GaugeSymmetries Gauge symmetries
          %p In this chapter we discuss these topics:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#CompactlySupportedInfinitesimalSymmetriesObstructTheCovariantPhaseSpace"} compactly supported infinitesimal symmetries obstruct covariant phase space
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InfinitesimalGauge"} Infinitesimal gauge symmetries
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#LieAlgebraActionAndLieAlgebroids"} Lie algebra action and Lie algebroids
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#BRSTComplex"} BRST complex
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#ExamplesForLocalBRSTComplexes"} Examples of local BRST complexes
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetry"} infinitesimal gauge symmetry
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeParameters"}
            below) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetry+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetry of the Lagrangian
            which may be freely parameterized, hence “gauged”, by a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameter"} gauge parameter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            exhibiting these is also called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
          %p
            By choosing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameter"} gauge parameter
            to have
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+support"} compact support
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
            in particular yield
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetries of the Lagrangian
            with compact spacetime support. One finds (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonTrivialImplicitInfinitesimalGaugeSymmetriesPbstructExistenceOfCauchySurfaces"}
            below) that the existence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
            non-trivial symmetries of this form is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            to the existence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            of the theory (prop.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CovariantPhaseSpace"}
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+symmetries"} gauge symmetries
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th name
                %th meaning
                %th def.
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetry+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetry of the Lagrangian
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evolutionary+vector+field"} evolutionary vector field
                  which leaves
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
                  up to a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+spacetime+derivative"} total spacetime derivative
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetriesAndConservedCurrents"}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  spacetime-compactly supported
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetry+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetry of the Lagrangian
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstructs
                  existence of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
                  (if non-trivial
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  prop.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonTrivialImplicitInfinitesimalGaugeSymmetriesPbstructExistenceOfCauchySurfaces"}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetry"} infinitesimal gauge symmetry
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameter"} gauge parameterized
                  collection of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetries of the Lagrangian
                  %br/
                  for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+support"} compactly supported
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameter"} gauge parameter
                  this yields spacetime-compactly supported infinitesimal symmetries
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeParameters"}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigid+infinitesimal+symmetry+of+the+Lagrangian"} rigid infinitesimal symmetry of the Lagrangian
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} infinitesimal symmetry modulo gauge symmetry
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RigidInfinitesimalSymmetriesOfTheLagrangian"}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  generating set of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameters"} gauge parameters
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  reflects all the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noether+identities"} Noether identities
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  remark
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingSetOfGaugeTransformations"}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  closed
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameters"} gauge parameters
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
                  closes on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameters"} gauge parameters
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeParametersClosed"}
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            But we may hard-wire these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+equivalences"} gauge equivalences
            into the very
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            by forming the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
            on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            is modeled by the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+Lie+algebroid"} action Lie algebroid
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ActionLieAlgebroid"}
            below). Its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
            is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+BRST+complex"} local BRST complex
            of the theory (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalOffShellBRSTComplex"}
          %p
            In this construction the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameters"} gauge parameters
            appear as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/auxiliary+fields"} auxiliary fields
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+manifold"} graded
            version of the
            = succeed "-bundle." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameter"} gauge parameter
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ghost+fields"} ghost fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
            themselves which leads to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ghost-of-ghost+fields"} ghost-of-ghost fields
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalBRSTComplexBFieldMinkowskiSpacetime"}
          %p
            It is these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/auxiliary+fields"} auxiliary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ghost+fields"} ghost fields
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ghost-of-ghost+fields"} ghost-of-ghost fields
