          %p
            The mathematical theory capturing these phenomena is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"} higher Lie theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E+algebroids"} Lie-∞ algebroids
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityAlgebroid"}
            below).
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p#CompactlySupportedInfinitesimalSymmetriesObstructTheCovariantPhaseSpace
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+support"} compactly supported
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetries
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruc
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
          %p
            As an immediate corollary of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FlowAlongInfinitesimalSymmetryOfLagrangianPreservesOnShellSpaceOfFieldHistories"}
            we have the following important observation:
          #NonTrivialImplicitInfinitesimalGaugeSymmetriesPbstructExistenceOfCauchySurfaces.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (spacetime-compactly supported and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
                non-trivial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetries of the Lagrangian
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruct
                the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\mathbf{L})
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"} Lorentzian
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %p
              If there exists a single
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetry+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetry of the Lagrangian
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetriesAndConservedCurrents"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it has compact spacetime support (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpacetimeSupport"}
              %li
                %p
                  it does not vanish
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ProlongedShellInJetBundle"} (?)
                  (so not a trivial one, example
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrivialImplicialInfinitesimalGaugeTransformations"}
            %p
              then there does not exist any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+surface"} Cauchy surface
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CauchySurface"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equations"} Euler-Lagrange
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerLagrangeEquationsOnTrivialVectorFieldBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FlowAlongInfinitesimalSymmetryOfLagrangianPreservesOnShellSpaceOfFieldHistories"}
              the flow along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat v
              preserves the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+histories"} space of field histories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat v
              does not vanish
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
              implies that this flow is non-trivial, hence that it does continuously change the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+histories"} field histories
              over some points of spacetime, while the assumption that it has compact spacetime support means that these changes are confined to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subset"} compact subset
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %p
              This means that there is a continuum of solutions to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              whose restriction to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
              of any
              = succeed "-1" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi p
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_p \hookrightarrow \Sigma
              outside of this compact support coincides. Therefore this restriction map is not an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_p
              not a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+surface"} Cauchy surface
              for the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
          %p
            Notice that there always exist spacetime-compactly supported infinitesimal symmetries that however do vanish
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
          #TrivialImplicialInfinitesimalGaugeTransformations.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (trivial compactly-supported
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetries of the Lagrangian
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\mathbf{L})
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MinkowskiSpacetime"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              is canonically of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo =
                    %mi L
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi dvol
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{L} = L \, dvol_\Sigma
            %p
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+function"} Lagrangian function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi J
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \in \Omega^{0,0}_\Sigma(E) = C^\infty(J^\infty_\Sigma(E))
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
              (characterized by prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JetBundleIsLocallyProManifold"}
            %p
              Then every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evolutionary+vector+field"} evolutionary vector field
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EvolutionaryVectorField"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              which is proportional to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+derivative"} Euler-Lagrange derivative
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EulerLagrangeEquationGeneral"} (?)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+function"} Lagrangian function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi EL
                        %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mi κ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi E
                      %mi ev
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi E
