              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            The following discussion introduces and uses the tremendously useful fact that (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"}> higher
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie theory
            may usefully be dually expressed in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebra"} differential graded-commutative algebra
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#differentialgradedcommutativeSuperalgebra"}
            below), namely in terms of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"}> Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
            ”. In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            literature, besides the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST-BV+formalism"} BRST-BV formalism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FDAs"}> FDAs
