                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left[ R(-) , R(-)\right]
                    \\;=\;
                    R([-,-]_{\mathcal{G}})
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the left we have the Lie bracket of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evolutionary+vector+fields"} evolutionary vector fields
              from prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EvolutionaryVectorFieldLieAlgebra"}
            %p
              Beware that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]_{\mathcal{G}}
              may be a function of the fields, namely of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameters"} gauge parameters
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]_{\mathcal{G}}
              in general defines a
              = succeed "-structure" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityAlgebroid"}
            %p
              Notice that the collection of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetries of the Lagrangian
              by necessity always forms a (very large)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+parameters"} gauge parameters
              is a condition on the
